 "description": "Compiler flags for each held-out case's translation unit, written from what the unit needs to parse (clang++ -fsyntax-only through scripts/run_real_bugs.py --tool syntax), before the checker ran on it. Placeholders and fields are those of corpus/real-bugs-heldout/commands.json. RAPIDS-based cases (cuOpt, spark-rapids-jni) take CCCL, NVTX and the RMM logger from the RMM 26.10 build of scripts/prepare_targets.py and load summaries of RMM's cuda_memcpy.cpp, cuda_stream_view.cpp and device_buffer.cpp as the RAPIDS cases there do (spark-rapids-jni also cuDF's cuda_memcpy.cu, as the cuDF development cases do). cuOpt takes RAFT and RMM at their last commit before the case revision on its RAPIDS_BRANCH; spark-rapids-jni takes cuDF at its thirdparty/cudf submodule commit and RMM at its last commit before the case revision. generatedHeaders rapids-logger holds RAFT's logger_macros.hpp (copied from corpus/real-bugs-heldout/generated) and cuOpt's cuopt/logger_macros.hpp, made the same way from logger_macros.hpp.in of the RMM 26.10 build's rapids_logger with the prefix CUOPT and default logger cuopt::default_logger() that cuOpt's cpp/CMakeLists.txt passes to create_logger_macros. generatedHeaders gromacs holds gromacs/libgromacs_export.h, the header CMake's generate_export_header(libgromacs) writes, with its standard content. cuCollections takes CCCL from the RMM 26.10 build (CUDA 13.2's CCCL 3.2 string_view deduction guides are rejected by Clang 23) and defines the macros nvcc predefines that cuco/detail/__config requires (__CUDACC_VER_MAJOR__/MINOR__ for CUDA 13.2, __CUDACC_EXTENDED_LAMBDA__ for the --expt-extended-lambda its tests use, __CUDA_ARCH_LIST__ for sm_89). instant-ngp takes its and tiny-cuda-nn's submodules at the recorded commits and CUDA 13.2's CCCL, with -std=c++17 (CCCL 3 requires it; the project builds with C++14). GROMACS cases are host C++ units of a CUDA build with thread-MPI; their config headers are generated by headerPatches.",
